(a) whether country could prevent a significant number of deaths by fully mitigating sulphur dioxide emissions from coal-fired power plants;
(b) if so, the salient features of the study conducted by researchers from IIT Delhi in this regard and published in the Nature journal recently;
(c) whether emissions have increased significantly on account of socio-economic changes and excessive dependency on coal; and
(d) if so, the steps on the anvil for stronger implementation of sulphur dioxide emission norms and prioritisation of hotspot regions?

(a) whether the country is witnessing large-scale curtailment of solar power as the grid struggles to absorb excess supply during the daytime;
